 ],
 "lineas": [
  {
   "texto": "Why does every sidewalk have lines cut into it every few feet?",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "Concrete shrinks as it dries, and it shrinks again every cold night.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "But the ground under it grips the slab, so the slab tears itself apart.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "A long slab will crack. There's no way to stop it.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "So builders cut a groove about a quarter of the way through.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "Now that line is the weakest spot, so the crack happens right there, hidden inside the groove.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "And when a tree root pushes up, only one square lifts, not the whole sidewalk.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "The cracks are still there. You just can't see them. Now you know.",
   "pausa": 0.2
  }
 ],
